Checked on 8 November 2026 (see licences.md): none of the 37 jar/aar archives behind the 84 runtime artifacts
(the rest are POM-only BOMs and Gradle-metadata redirects) ships a NOTICE file, so Apache 2.0 section 4(d) requires no text to be reproduced beyond this list. Re-run
scripts/licences.sh on every dependency change, and re-check for NOTICE files in the resolved jars/aars:
if a dependency adds one, its text must be copied here verbatim.

Apache 2.0 section 4 duties for a distributed binary, for the person selling the app:
  (a) give recipients a copy of the licence: ship LICENSE (or the licence text) inside the app, for example
      on an "Open source licences" screen reachable from the app, or link to it in the store listing;
  (b) keep modified files marked as changed, if any third-party Apache file is modified (none is today);
  (c) keep copyright, patent, trademark and attribution notices in any source redistributed;
  (d) reproduce the contents of each dependency's NOTICE file, if it has one (none today).
The app currently has no in-app licences screen: that is a gap to close before it is sold (finding L-1 of
docs/security/review-2026-11-08.md).
